// A text/event-stream of one organization's events only. Each committed item event arrives as `event: item` with `id:` the event id and `data:` a StreamEvent. Other event names (definition, factory, connection, knowledge) carry their own data object; clients ignore the names they do not know. `event: definition` (data a DefinitionEvent, no id) follows every committed change of a factory's definition: a factory created or deleted, its current version moved (publish, restore, pause, resume), its draft opened, saved, discarded or published. `event: factory` (data a FactoryEvent, no id) follows a change of a factory's line that is not an item's: its andon cord pulled or cleared. `event: connection` (data a ConnectionEvent, no id) follows a connection created, changed, tested or deleted. `event: knowledge` (data a KnowledgeEvent, no id) follows a knowledge source's sync starting or ending. `event: resync` (data `{}`) means goald may have missed events (it reconnected to the database): re-read what you show. A comment line (`: heartbeat`) arrives every 15 seconds. There is no replay: Last-Event-ID is ignored, so a client that reconnects re-reads what it shows. goald ends the stream of a client that falls too far behind.
